        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_706bc37620ef4242983cd742f21d6b58",
      "statement": "Both test methods are wrapped in test-managed transactions that Spring rolls back: delete() loads every Category row through DetachedCriteria and calls dao.delete on each, while test() only inserts when the table is already empty — which never happens after dbInit seeds category — and its (++i) loop would in any case create five rows while printing a message claiming ten.",
